  "limitations": [
    "Production forwarding stays disabled; these tests use the explicit development tag where required. No browser trust installation, Basic fallback or new remote authority is introduced.",
    "Source authentication proves possession of the pinned mesh signing identity, not the identity of an operating-system process or application. Existing legacy plaintext callers retain their prior port-handoff bearer risk and are not source-authenticated clients.",
    "The original listener owns a certificate snapshot. A later certificate renewal makes current CLI pins refuse that older snapshot until the listener is restarted; no silent certificate adoption occurs.",
    "Existing Manager join/recovery unit fixtures use controlled resource observations. Actual compiled three-daemon workflows use unmodified native availability collectors on hosted macOS arm64 and Ubuntu amd64; no CPU observation override is used for them.",
    "Source Stop may retain a charge while exact port reclamation remains unresolved. The public fixture explicitly retains that state and requires original-process exit, exclusive ownership and exact-key recovery rather than reporting premature settlement.",
    "This accepts scoped source-binding integration, not the complete forwarding specification. Native suspend-aware remaining-time guards, broader route-loss/resource-credit/platform/UI/formal gates remain separate work.",
    "All selected cases passed without skips. The native fallback queue was cancelled before a validation child started and supplies no test result. Raw receipts remain outside version control or in expiring CI artifacts; normalized rosters, exits, source/image hashes and public references are retained here."
  ],
